cherAssistant.nav.teacher":"Penguin Teacher Assistant","teacherAssistant.prompt.classroomQuestioning.coreQuestions":"For senior-high history \"Monarchical Autocracy in the Ming and Qing\", distill one or two core questions that can command the whole lesson and drive inquiry.","teacherAssistant.prompt.classroomQuestioning.followUpPrompts":"For junior-high math \"The Sum of Interior Angles of a Triangle\", prepare a set of follow-up scripts to guide students to the answer step by step when they get stuck.","teacherAssistant.prompt.classroomQuestioning.openEndedQuestions":"Turn the closed, right-or-wrong-only questions in primary Chinese \"The Destruction of the Old Summer Palace\" into open-ended questions that provoke thinking and discussion.","teacherAssistant.prompt.classroomQuestioning.questionChain":"For junior-high physics Atmospheric Pressure, design a question chain from shallow to deep, guiding students' thinking step by step from context-based introduction to core inquiry.","teacherAssistant.prompt.classroomQuestioning.responseGuidance":"For junior-high biology Ecosystems, design a set of response scripts to use after a student answers correctly — pressing one layer further to dig the knowledge point deeper.","teacherAssistant.prompt.coursewareCreation.experimentCourseware":"For junior-high chemistry \"Combustion and Fire Extinguishing\", make a set of experimental-inquiry courseware, including experiment steps, observation records and conclusion analysis.","teacherAssistant.prompt.coursewareCreation.lessonPlanToCourseware":"Turn the full lesson plan of junior-high Chinese \"The Sight of Father's Back\" into a complete set of screen-ready courseware, with a corresponding page for each teaching phase.","teacherAssistant.prompt.coursewareCreation.newLessonCourseware":"For junior-high physics Ohm's Law, make a full set of new-content-lesson courseware, including context-based introduction, new-knowledge instruction, breakthrough of key and difficult points, in-class practice and summary.","teacherAssistant.prompt.coursewareCreation.openClassCourseware":"For primary Chinese \"The Destruction of the Old Summer Palace\", make a set of open-class courseware with refined layout, prominent key and difficult points, and emotional resonance.","teacherAssistant.prompt.coursewareCreation.reviewCourseware":"For junior-high math \"Linear Equations in One Variable\", make a set of unit-review courseware that organizes the knowledge network, typical worked examples and error-prone points.","teacherAssistant.prompt.creativeTeaching.crossDisciplinaryTheme":"Turn primary science \"The Three States of Water\" into an interdisciplinary thematic learning unit; specify which subjects are involved, what outcomes students produce, and the class-hour arrangement.","teacherAssistant.prompt.creativeTeaching.inquiryLessonDesign":"Turn senior-high chemistry \"Iron and Its Compounds\" into an inquiry lesson centered on students' hands-on experiments; specify how each inquiry activity is organized.","teacherAssistant.prompt.creativeTeaching.multiPlanSelection":"For junior-high math Linear Functions, give three teaching plans — project-based, context-based and inquiry-based — each with its features and the class situations it suits, for me to choose from.","teacherAssistant.prompt.creativeTeaching.projectBasedDesign":"For junior-high physics Buoyancy, design a project-based learning plan built around the authentic task of \"designing load capacity for a ship\"; specify the task, inquiry stages and outcomes.","teacherAssistant.prompt.creativeTeaching.situatedLessonDesign":"For junior-high biology \"Photosynthesis\", design a context-based lesson that carries students through with one authentic context and driving question running across the whole class.","teacherAssistant.prompt.differentiatedHomework.extensionHomework":"For more capable students, design an extension-inquiry homework for junior-high physics \"Buoyancy\" — challenging yet within the syllabus.","teacherAssistant.prompt.differentiatedHomework.homeworkDifficultyLabeling":"For this set of junior-high chemistry Acids and Bases homework, label each item with its difficulty tier and estimated completion time.","teacherAssistant.prompt.differentiatedHomework.homeworkStreamlining":"Redesign the high-volume, repetitive homework of senior-high English Unit 1, covering the core objectives with fewer, finer questions — less quantity, no quality loss.","teacherAssistant.prompt.differentiatedHomework.homeworkTimeControl":"Compress the over-length homework for primary Chinese *Watching the Tide* into the required time, cutting mechanical repetition without lowering quality.","teacherAssistant.prompt.differentiatedHomework.tieredHomework":"Per the \"Double Reduction\" requirements, design three tiers of flexible homework — basic, developmental and extension — for junior-high math Linear Equations in One Variable, labeling difficulty and estimated time.","teacherAssistant.prompt.differentiatedTeaching.advancedExtensionTask":"For more capable students, design an extension-challenge task for senior-high math Sequences — raising difficulty while staying centered on core knowledge.","teacherAssistant.prompt.differentiatedTeaching.differentiatedLearningPath":"For the reading and appreciation of junior-high Chinese \"Spring\", design differentiated learning paths so both weaker students and more capable ones can reach a little beyond their grasp.","teacherAssistant.prompt.differentiatedTeaching.learningSupportScaffold":"For a struggling student learning primary math *Two-Digit by Two-Digit Multiplication*, design a learning scaffold with hints, worked examples and step-by-step guidance.","teacherAssistant.prompt.differentiatedTeaching.tieredGroupingPlan":"For junior-high physics \"Circuit Connection\", design a tiered grouping plan for classroom organization; specify how to group, the task differences across groups, and how they flow.","teacherAssistant.prompt.differentiatedTeaching.tieredTaskDesign":"For junior-high math The Pythagorean Theorem, design three tiers of learning tasks — basic, intermediate and advanced — specifying the goal each tier should reach.","teacherAssistant.prompt.homeSchoolCommunication.concernMessage":"Help me phrase a message to tell a parent that their child is inattentive in class — affirm first, then show concern, then give advice — without escalating conflict.","teacherAssistant.prompt.homeSchoolCommunication.parentCooperationRequest":"Write a communication script asking the parent to help supervise 20 minutes of daily extracurricular reading, without making it feel like a burden.","teacherAssistant.prompt.homeSchoolCommunication.praiseFeedback":"Write a specific praise feedback to a parent: this week the child proactively helped a classmate with problems and improved markedly — use examples rather than vague praise.","teacherAssistant.prompt.homeSchoolCommunication.sensitiveTopicCommunication":"Help me get the wording right for discussing signs of a child's puppy love with the parent — stating it clearly without hurting feelings.","teacherAssistant.prompt.homeSchoolCommunication.wordingRefinement":"Rewrite \"Your child keeps not handing in homework lately, please do something\" to be more tactful and easier for the parent to accept.","teacherAssistant.prompt.homeworkReview.errorCauseAnalysis":"Categorize this batch of junior-high math Factorization errors by cause, identify the whole-class common problems, and point out which categories to focus on.","teacherAssistant.prompt.homeworkReview.reviewLessonDesign":"For senior-high physics \"Force Analysis\", design a review lesson; specify which problems to focus on, how to explain them, and how to help students draw inferences.","teacherAssistant.prompt.homeworkReview.reviewPriority":"From this batch of junior-high Chinese sentence-correction homework, pick the few common problems most worth explaining — review right where it counts.","teacherAssistant.prompt.homeworkReview.transferApplication":"For the common error in junior-high physics \"misapplying the speed formula\", design an authentic-context transfer problem to check mastery.","teacherAssistant.prompt.homeworkReview.variationExerciseSet":"Around the high-frequency error in junior-high math \"absolute-value simplification\", create a set of variant problems that change contexts and phrasings to consolidate learning.","teacherAssistant.prompt.learningSituationAnalysis.academicQualityProfile":"Produce an academic-quality profile of this class's math learning — stating strengths, weaknesses and development trends.","teacherAssistant.prompt.learningSituationAnalysis.examQualityAnalysis":"From difficulty and discrimination, analyze the item-setting quality of this junior-high physics paper and where the class's answering problems lie.","teacherAssistant.prompt.learningSituationAnalysis.knowledgePointDiagnosis":"Based on the scoring rate of each knowledge point, judge which content Grade-9 chemistry should focus on next and how to make it up.","teacherAssistant.prompt.learningSituationAnalysis.learningSituationReport":"Based on this Grade-8 math monthly-exam scores, produce a standard learning-situation analysis report with overall status, problem diagnosis and teaching suggestions.","teacherAssistant.prompt.learningSituationAnalysis.scoreCauseAnalysis":"Read out the problems behind this English score data and give a few teaching adjustments that can land immediately.","teacherAssistant.prompt.lessonPlanWriting.blackboardDesignAndReflection":"For primary Chinese \"Study for the Rise of China\", design the teaching board layout and add a post-lesson teaching reflection.","teacherAssistant.prompt.lessonPlanWriting.learningGuide":"Turn junior-high math \"Properties of Parallelograms\" into a guided learning plan + learning sheet + assessment sheet, so students can follow along in class and be tested on the spot.","teacherAssistant.prompt.lessonPlanWriting.lessonPlanCompletion":"For the lesson plan of junior-high history \"The Opium War\", complete the missing textbook analysis, learning-situation analysis and the design rationale of each phase.","teacherAssistant.prompt.lessonPlanWriting.situatedLessonPlan":"For junior-high chemistry \"Combustion and Fire Extinguishing\", write a lesson plan that incorporates authentic context and disciplinary practice, letting students learn more by doing.","teacherAssistant.prompt.lessonPlanWriting.standardLessonPlan":"Turn the ins
b00
tructional design of primary Chinese \"Borrowing Arrows with Straw Boats\" into a standard, fully-elemented lesson plan ready to teach.","teacherAssistant.prompt.openClassDesign.competitionStandardAlignment":"Against the teaching-contest scoring rubric, see where the junior-high English \"object clauses\" open class still falls short and how to make up for a high score.","teacherAssistant.prompt.openClassDesign.highlightSessionDesign":"For the open class junior-high physics *The Production and Propagation of Sound*, design highlight and climax phases that make observing teachers sit up.","teacherAssistant.prompt.openClassDesign.lessonPresentationScript":"For primary math \"Understanding Clocks\", write a well-structured lesson-presentation script covering the textbook, learning situation, pedagogy and process.","teacherAssistant.prompt.openClassDesign.regularLessonUpgrade":"Polish the regular lesson junior-high Chinese \"The Sight of Father's Back\" into an open class that holds up to scrutiny; specify where to add highlights and how to upgrade.","teacherAssistant.prompt.openClassDesign.teachingRehearsalReview":"For the open class senior-high chemistry Chemical Equilibrium, design how to do the trial teaching and from which angles to review and polish afterward.","teacherAssistant.prompt.paperWriting.academicExpressionRefinement":"Rewrite the colloquial line \"I think this method works pretty well and students like it too\" to be more academic and standardized.","teacherAssistant.prompt.paperWriting.empiricalPaperWriting":"Turn the outcome of the topic \"applying mind maps in junior-high biology review\" into a publishable empirical research paper.","teacherAssistant.prompt.paperWriting.journalSubmissionAdvice":"Advise which type of education journal the paper \"unit-holistic instructional design\" suits, and what to watch for in submission.","teacherAssistant.prompt.paperWriting.paperStructureRevision":"Look over the structure and logic of the paper *A Practical Study of Group Cooperative Learning* and help me make it more rigorous.","teacherAssistant.prompt.paperWriting.rejectionRiskReview":"From a reviewer's perspective, point out the problems in the paper *Application of Context-Based Teaching* that could lead to rejection, and help me revise.","teacherAssistant.prompt.parentMeetingMaterials.familyEducationAdvice":"Prepare a few specific, actionable family-education suggestions for parents of junior-high students, usable the moment they get home.","teacherAssistant.prompt.parentMeetingMaterials.parentMeetingPlanning":"Plan this Grade-7 new-student parent meeting as a whole — produce the agenda, speech and accompanying courseware.","teacherAssistant.prompt.parentMeetingMaterials.parentMeetingSpeech":"Write a mid-term Grade-8 parent-meeting speech, including ope
